    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0139" n="130" xml:id="pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/959: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Pell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-21T18:00:00+01:00">June 21, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 21—3:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>81. Referring to the Legation’s telegram No. 76, June 19, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="98"
                        xml:id="d167-f1"/> informed now from Bordeaux and Madrid that at least 600
                    or 700 American refugees awaiting repatriation most of these expecting to come
                    through Lisbon. Lisbon housing facilities exhausted, Portuguese Government will
                    not permit transit unless we can guarantee a ship. They are also giving
                    preference in over-crowded conditions to British, Dutch and Belgian refugees who
                    would be liable to internment in France. Urge again that <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Manhattan</hi> or other ship be sent at once and that announcements be made
                    that it will call at Lisbon, Bilbao and if possible St. Jean de Luz. Again
                    repeat Portuguese Government having several hundred thousand visa applications
                    and a food shortage in prospect cannot justly be asked to grant anything but
                    strictly transit facilities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
